            <ArticleTitle>Post-herpetic trigeminal neuralgia treated with deep brain stimulation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>512-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Post-herpetic neuralgic affects up to 20% of patients after an attack of trigeminal Herpes Zoster infection. Past medical and surgical treatments have been unrewarding. We report the successful treatment of such a case with deep brain stimulation into the region of the contralateral periventricular grey area (PVG) and ventral posterior lateral thalamic nucleus (VPL).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
